 To find the slope of the line, we first solve the system of equations for $x$ and $y$:
\[
\begin{align*}
x + 2y &= 7t + 3 \\
x - y &= 2t - 2
\end{align*}
\]
Now subtract the second equation from the first to eliminate $x$:
\[
\begin{align*}
(x + 2y) - (x - y) &= (7t + 3) - (2t - 2) \\
3y &= 5t + 5 \\
y &= \frac{5}{3}t + \frac{5}{3}
\end{align*}
\]
Substitute this expression for $y$ into one of the original equations to solve for $x$:
\[
\begin{align*}
x - \left(\frac{5}{3}t + \frac{5}{3}\right) &= 2t - 2 \\
x &= 2t - 2 + \frac{5}{3}t + \frac{5}{3} \\
&= \frac{11}{3}t - \frac{1}{3}
\end{align*}
\]
We have $x = \frac{11}{3}t - \frac{1}{3}$ and $y = \frac{5}{3}t + \frac{5}{3}$. The slope of the line is the ratio of the change in $y$ to the change in $x$, which is $\frac{dy}{dx} = \frac{\frac{5}{3}}{\frac{11}{3}} = \frac{5}{11}$. </think> <answer> \frac{5}{11} </answer>
